</span><div class="gd-t">Post it. Then press <b class="gd-ui">Posted</b> on Today and paste the listing&#39;s address. Press <b class="gd-ui">Renewed</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Updated</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Taken down</b> the same way when you do those.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Inbox replies for this car</b> has the answers for price, availability, requirements, deposit, delivery and &quot;send your number&quot;, filled in for the car. Each one ends with the car&#39;s link or asks for a phone number.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">6</span><div class="gd-t">After answering the inbox, open <b class="gd-ui">Log an inbox session</b>. Enter the number of chats and the numbers collected, one per line (name, phone, car code). Each new number becomes a lead, and customer service gets a call-back task due within 15 minutes.</div></li></ol></div><ul class="gd-ul"><li>Kits are made when the page opens, so their prices are today&#39;s. A price change marks the live listing <b class="gd-ui">Update the price</b> and opens the usual update task.</li><li>A car that does not take requests, has no daily rate or has only sample photos says <b class="gd-ui">Do not post yet</b>.</li><li><b class="gd-ui">Rotation settings</b> change the posts a day, the days before a renewal, and the default location (a car&#39;s home area wins).</li><li>The booking request asks &quot;How did you hear about us?&quot; (optional). Bookings by channel counts the answer after staff&#39;s source and a tracked visit.</li></ul></section><section class="gd-task" id="advertising-and-owner-recruitment-write-an-ad" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Write an ad</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Marketing</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Listings</b>.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Choose the car and the channel (Facebook Marketplace, Kijiji, Craigslist, Instagram, Facebook Page or Google Business Profile) and press <b class="gd-ui">Write it</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Copy each part with its button: the title, the price line, the description (or caption), the hashtags and the tracked link. Each shows its length against the channel&#39;s limit (a Kijiji title takes 64 characters, Craigslist 70, an Instagram caption 2,200, a Google post 1,500).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Add the photos in the order shown: the first is the cover. Open a photo to save it.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Post the ad on the site, then press <b class="gd-ui">Mark as posted</b> and paste its address and the date.</div></li></ol></div><ul class="gd-ul"><li>The text comes from the car&#39;s record only: the rates, kilometres, deposit, delivery fee, who may rent it and the car code. A fact the record does not have is left out. No review, rating or claim is added.</li><li>The tracked link opens the car&#39;s page with utm_source (the channel), utm_medium and utm_campaign (the car code), so the request counts under that channel.</li><li>A warning shows when the car does not take requests, has no daily rate, or shows sample photos (take real photos first: an ad shows the car itself).</li><li>Facebook Marketplace is posted from the owner&#39;s own Facebook profile in their browser: Meta does not take vehicle listings from business Pages. Kijiji takes one ad per car, in one category and one region. An Instagram caption cannot hold a working link: put it in the bio or a story link sticker.</li></ul></section><section class="gd-task" id="advertising-and-owner-recruitment-when-an-ad-needs-updating" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">When an ad needs updating</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Marketing</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Posted ads</b>, or the task in <b class="gd-ui">Today</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Staff tasks</b>.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">A change of 3% or more in a car&#39;s daily, weekend, weekly or 30-day rate, any change of its deposit, kilometres, extra-km price or delivery fee, or the car leaving the site marks each of its live ads Needs updating and opens a task for the sales assistants (for example Update the Kijiji ad and the car). The task says what changed, the new price line and the ad&#39;s address.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">New text</b>, copy the new text and update the ad on the site.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Mark the ad updated</b>. The task closes. Closing the task in Staff tasks counts too.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Car off the site: take the ad down and press <b class="gd-ui">Taken down</b>. If the car comes back at the same rates first, the task is cancelled by itself.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>The 3% is under <b class="gd-ui">Settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Program</b>, Advertising and owner recruitment. The rates are checked again every 6 hours, so a rate dated ahead is caught on its day.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="advertising-and-owner-recruitment-bookings-by-channel" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Bookings by channel</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Marketing</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Bookings by channel</b>.</p><ul class="gd-ul"><li>Every request of the dates chosen counts once: under the source staff set on the booking, else the renter&#39;s visit (the campaign source of a tracked link, or the site they came from), else a referral code, else how it reached us (phone, email, WhatsApp).</li><li>Choose the last visit before the request or the first visit. A booking is a request that was confirmed, paid or completed; revenue is its rental charge after discounts. The months add up to the Bookings list.</li><li>The visit is kept with the request when it is sent, so the source outlives the 90 days of visit history. A visitor who refused analytics cookies has no source.</li><li>On a booking, the line Came from shows the source. Press <b class="gd-ui">Set</b> to give it by hand when the renter told you (a Kijiji reply, a walk-in, word of mouth).</li></ul></section><section class="gd-task" id="advertising-and-owner-recruitment-facebook-page-and-instagram-drafts" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Facebook Page and Instagram drafts</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Marketing</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Social drafts</b>.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">The week&#39;s drafts are written from the fleet every 6 hours, for this week and the next: Monday a new car (published in the last 14 days) or a featured one; Tuesday the owner program; Thursday the cars free this weekend; Friday the requirements (Instagram); Sunday a price highlight or a seasonal trip (Facebook Page). Press <b class="gd-ui">Write drafts for this week</b> to write them now.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Read each draft. Press <b class="gd-ui">Edit</b> to change the caption, the channels or the day, then <b class="gd-ui">Approve</b>; or press <b class="gd-ui">Skip</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Copy the caption for each channel (on the Facebook Page the tracked link is in the text; for Instagram copy the link for the bio), post it with the photos shown, then press <b class="gd-ui">Posted on Instagram</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Posted on Facebook Page</b> and paste the post&#39;s address.</div></li></ol></div><ul class="gd-ul"><li>Wednesday&#39;s walkaround video and Saturday&#39;s handover story are filmed by field staff. No renter is shown without written consent.</li><li>Press <b class="gd-ui">Add a post of your own</b> at the bottom of the week for anything else.</li></ul></section><section class="gd-task" id="advertising-and-owner-recruitment-meta-publishing-off-until-set-up" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Meta publishing (off until set up)</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Meta publishing</b>. Until it is on, every post is copied and posted by hand.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Make the Instagram account a professional account and link it to the CarmaCars Facebook Page.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">At developers.facebook.com, create a Business app owned by the CarmaCars business portfolio. Give it the permissions pages_show_list, pages_read_engagement, pages_manage_posts, instagram_basic and instagram_content_publish, and make a long-lived Page access token. Meta may ask for App Review before posts are public.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Enter the details</b>: the Page id, the Instagram account id and the token. The token goes to the vault; the page shows only its last four characters.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Switch on</b>. Approved drafts then go out on their day and their post links are recorded; a refusal shows on the draft. Press <b class="gd-ui">Switch off</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Remove the token</b> at any time.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="advertising-and-owner-recruitment-owner-recruitment" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Owner recruitment</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Marketing</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Owner recruitment</b>.</p><p class="gd-p">Owners and co-hosts are found in classified ads. The anti-spam law (CASL) does not cover a live phone call, but an email or a text needs consent, names the sender and offers an unsubscribe. The lawyer confirms the approach before outreach starts.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Add a lead</b>: paste the ad&#39;s address, choose who is selling (a private seller, a dealer or a rental business) and type the name, the phone and the car from the ad. Nothing is collected from the classified site.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Call them with the script on the lead&#39;s page and press <b class="gd-ui">Log the call</b>. A yes needs their words (&quot;Yes, text me the details&quot;): they become express consent in the log. A no means do not contact, ever.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">When the lead&#39;s page says email or text is allowed, choose a template, check the words and press <b class="gd-ui">Send</b>. The email adds CarmaCars&#39; name, mailing address and the unsubscribe link; the text ends with &quot;Reply STOP to opt out.&quot; Texts wait for 8 am during quiet hours.</div></li></ol></div><ul class="gd-ul"><li>Press <b class="gd-ui">Record consent</b> for consent given another way: express (with its proof), implied by their inquiry (6 months), implied by a business relationship (2 years), a business address published with no &quot;no solicitation&quot; note (never a private seller), or one message after a referral (naming the referrer).</li><li>The consent log is never edited: a change is a new line. An unsubscribe or a STOP reply adds a withdrawal by itself, and nothing more goes on that channel.</li><li>A message without consent is refused with the reason. <b class="gd-ui">Settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Program</b> has a switch that stops all recruitment messages.</li></ul><aside class="gd-box gd-box--warn"><span class="gd-lbl">Watch out</span><div>Keep the proof of an oral yes: a recording, or a note written during the call with the time. Consent you cannot show does not count.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="advertising-and-owner-recruitment-owner-pipeline" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Owner pipeline</h2><p class="gd-p">Open <b class="gd-ui">Marketing</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Owner pipeline</b>. Every prospective owner is one card, in one of seven columns: New, Contacted, Call booked, Agreement sent, Signed, Car onboarded and Lost. Leads come from the owner form on the website, an owner&#39;s referral link, Owner recruitment (classified ads) and <b class="gd-ui">Add an owner lead</b>.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Follow-up emails go by themselves on day 0, 2, 5 and 10 after a lead comes in: the owner program in plain words (the car goes on our fleet insurance policy, we rent it out in Toronto and pay the owner every month; fees apply) and the link to apply. They are marketing emails: they wait behind every other email under the daily limit, go in the sending hours and carry the unsubscribe link.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">They go only with consent: a website inquiry counts for 6 months, a classified-ad lead needs consent in its log, and a referral typed by staff gets one message only.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">They stop when the lead replies (a text or a call from their number, or press <b class="gd-ui">They replied</b>), when the stage changes, when they unsubscribe, and after the last one. <b class="gd-ui">Stop follow-ups</b> and <b class="gd-ui">Restart follow-ups</b> are on each card.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Move</b> changes the stage (with a note, and why when lost). Agreement sent, Signed and Car onboarded also follow the owner&#39;s records: an owner agreement sent or signed, a car on the site.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">Sales and Customer service see the same board in the staff portal.</div></li></ol></div><h3 class="gd-h3">Owner referral links</h3><p class="gd-p">An owner&#39;s link for new owners is <span class="gd-url">carmacars.ca/r/&lt;their code&gt;?to=owner</span> (the list is at the bottom of the board). A new owner who applies after it is credited to that owner. The credit follows the referral kickback rule: the Kickback Rate (20%) of the Rental Charge of the first completed rental of the new owner&#39;s car. It shows under <b class="gd-ui">Owner referral credits</b> as due; pay it with the owner&#39;s payout and press <b class="gd-ui">Mark paid</b>.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="advertising-and-owner-recruitment-listing-channels" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Listing channels</h2><p class="gd-p">Open <b class="gd-ui">Marketing</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Listing channels</b>: the sites and directories where our cars can be listed beyond carmacars.ca (Turo, Getaround, Google Business Profile, Google Merchant Center, the Meta catalog, Kijiji, Facebook Marketplace, KAYAK, Expedia, Discover Cars, Rentalcars.com, Craigslist, Bing Places, Apple Business Connect, Yelp, YellowPages and any you add).</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Each has a status (Not started, Applied, Live, Paused, Not for us), who holds the login, notes and how listing works there. Press <b class="gd-ui">Update</b> to change them, <b class="gd-ui">Add a channel</b> for a new one.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">None is connected by itself: apply on the site. When a site or partner program takes a feed, give it that channel&#39;s address: <b class="gd-ui">JSON</b>, <b class="gd-ui">CSV</b> or <b class="gd-ui">XML</b> (the XML is in the shape of Google&#39;s vehicle listings feed). Car links carry the channel, so its bookings show in Bookings by channel.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Every feed has our own and co-hosted cars on the site, never a partner&#39;s car (01 Motors or any other). <b class="gd-ui">Keep out</b> takes a car out of every feed.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">New key</b> ends the old address. Each feed is read at most 60 times an hour and each answer is kept 15 minutes.</div></li></ol></div></section>');
select app.guide_release_section('admin', 'the-investor-deck', 'chapter', 'add-ons', 'The investor deck is a slide deck in the investor portal at `/investor/deck`. Signed-in investors see it while it is shown; Admins always see it. Its figures come from the database when it opens: the owner fee tiers, the partner commission, the real cars'' public rates, delivery, add-ons and renter fees, the deductible and deposits, and the investment terms of Program settings.

## Preview and settings

1. Go to **Investors** and press **Investor deck**. The button says whether investors see it now.
2. The page shows the settings, then the whole deck as investors see it.
3. **Show the deck to investors**: on, investors see it under Investor deck and on their Investments page; off, only Admins see it.
4. **Multiplier on the money we invest (x)**: the company''s own figure, shown large on the profitability slide with its footnote (internal, not audited).
5. **Yearly percentage of the current offer (%)**: used by the worked examples and the calculator. Each investor''s own percentage is the one in their agreement.
6. Press **Save deck settings**. Every change is in the audit log.

To hide or show it in one click, use **Hide the deck from investors** or **Show the deck to investors** on Investors.

How we make money is one slide with the seven revenue lines: our own cars, owners'' cars fully managed with coverage under our fleet policy, coverage under our fleet policy for owners who manage their own cars, Turo management, brokering partner fleets with the chauffeur service, detailing, and the body shop. The features include maintenance and service tracking, phone number sign-in, saving contacts from unfinished forms and smart Turo car matching, and the newest: the redesigned renter, owner, investor, assistant, field and Admin screens, terms car by car, deposits settled after the bills come in, offers and rentals added fast, the staff assistant, and promo code end dates. Their screens in the deck are real screens with fictional people.

> Good to know: The deck shows no internal costs, fleet counts or staff pay. Every example is labelled as an illustration, with the forward-looking statements notice on every slide and in the PDF.
', 'The investor deck', 'Preview the deck, show or hide it, and set its multiplier and percentage.',
  'The investor deck is a slide deck in the investor portal at `/investor/deck`. Signed-in investors see it while it is shown; Admins always see it. Its figures come from the database when it opens: the owner fee tiers, the partner commission, the real cars'' public rates, delivery, add-ons and renter fees, the deductible and deposits, and the investment terms of Program settings.

## Preview and settings

1. Go to **Investors** and press **Investor deck**. The button says whether investors see it now.
2. The page shows the settings, then the whole deck as investors see it.
3. **Show the deck to investors**: on, investors see it under Investor deck and on their Investments page; off, only Admins see it.
4. **Multiplier on the money we invest (x)**: the company''s own figure, shown large on the profitability slide with its footnote (internal, not audited).
5. **Yearly percentage of the current offer (%)**: used by the worked examples and the calculator. Each investor''s own percentage is the one in their agreement.
6. Press **Save deck settings**. Every change is in the audit log.

To hide or show it in one click, use **Hide the deck from investors** or **Show the deck to investors** on Investors.

How we make money is one slide with the seven revenue lines: our own cars, owners'' cars fully managed with coverage under our fleet policy, coverage under our fleet policy for owners who manage their own cars, Turo management, brokering partner fleets with the chauffeur service, detailing, and the body shop. The feature slides follow the platform as it is today. For renters: the rental walkthrough, CarmaCars Rewards, and Add to calendar and Apple Wallet. For owners: flat monthly pay per car as well as revenue share. For the team: one staff portal for every function, the training academy, the card reader and card payments, and insurer billing. Admin and automation: e-signatures everywhere with an audit trail, phone and browser alerts, and the live map. Growth: listing channels and feeds, the owner pipeline, and Facebook Marketplace kits. Their screens are real screens with fictional people; a feature with no screen shows how it works.

> Good to know: The deck shows no internal costs, fleet counts or staff pay. Every example is labelled as an illustration, with the forward-looking statements notice on every slide and in the PDF.
',
  '<p class="gd-p">The investor deck is a slide deck in the investor portal at <span class="gd-url">/investor/deck</span>. Signed-in investors see it while it is shown; Admins always see it. Its figures come from the database when it opens: the owner fee tiers, the partner commission, the real cars&#39; public rates, delivery, add-ons and renter fees, the deductible and deposits, and the investment terms of Program settings.</p><section class="gd-task" id="the-investor-deck-preview-and-settings" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Preview and settings</h2><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Go to <b class="gd-ui">Investors</b> and press <b class="gd-ui">Investor deck</b>. The button says whether investors see it now.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">The page shows the settings, then the whole deck as investors see it.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Show the deck to investors</b>: on, investors see it under Investor deck and on their Investments page; off, only Admins see it.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Multiplier on the money we invest (x)</b>: the company&#39;s own figure, shown large on the profitability slide with its footnote (internal, not audited).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Yearly percentage of the current offer (%)</b>: used by the worked examples and the calculator. Each investor&#39;s own percentage is the one in their agreement.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">6</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Save deck settings</b>. Every change is in the audit log.</div></li></ol></div><p class="gd-p">To hide or show it in one click, use <b class="gd-ui">Hide the deck from investors</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Show the deck to investors</b> on Investors.</p><p class="gd-p">How we make money is one slide with the seven revenue lines: our own cars, owners&#39; cars fully managed with coverage under our fleet policy, coverage under our fleet policy for owners who manage their own cars, Turo management, brokering partner fleets with the chauffeur service, detailing, and the body shop. The feature slides follow the platform as it is today. For renters: the rental walkthrough, CarmaCars Rewards, and Add to calendar and Apple Wallet. For owners: flat monthly pay per car as well as revenue share. For the team: one staff portal for every function, the training academy, the card reader and card payments, and insurer billing. Admin and automation: e-signatures everywhere with an audit trail, phone and browser alerts, and the live map. Growth: listing channels and feeds, the owner pipeline, and Facebook Marketplace kits. Their screens are real screens with fictional people; a feature with no screen shows how it works.</p><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>The deck shows no internal costs, fleet counts or staff pay. Every example is labelled as an illustration, with the forward-looking statements notice on every slide and in the PDF.</div></aside></section>');
